ined, dark-green with slight pinkish bronze flush to margins and veins in spring, colouring orange-red in autumn. Small green flower heads surrounded by four slender, pointed, pink bracts, which may range from deep red to almost white are borne in summer. Strawberry-like red fruit develop in autumn.","image":"visi148438.jpg","commonName":"kousa 'Dwarf Pink'","nurseriesCount":2,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":178921,"botanicalName":"<em>Cornus</em> <em>kousa</em> 'Ed Mezitt'","entityDescription":"A large deciduous shrub or small tree to 5m in height. New branches are purple, young leaves purple until flowering, changing to green. Slender stellate bracts start greenish and slightly pink and lighten to pure white, surrounding a small green flowerhead, in June. These are followed by strawberry like fruits in late summer.","image":"moja08105.jpg","commonName":"kousa 'Ed Mezitt'","nurseriesCount":3,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":133748,"botanicalName":"<em>Cornus</em> <em>kousa</em> 'Elizabeth Lustgarten'","entityDescription":"A small, angular tree with a stem which lies flat on the ground, with horizontal main branches to 3-4m in height. Leaves green with occasional bronze tints and good autumn colour. Petal-like broad, overlapping bracts, white tinged pink at maturity surround a greenish flower head. Red strawberry-like fruits appear in autumn.","image":"","commonName":"kousa 'Elizabeth Lustgarten'","nurseriesCount":2,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":233353,"botanicalName":"<em>Cornus</em> <em>kousa</em> 'Eurostar'","entityDescription":"A shrub or compact small tree to 2-3m in height. Leaves shiny dark green with paler midvein, with good autumn colour. Plentiful blooms of blousy, white, overlapping petal-like, medium-sized bracts attractively fading to red at the margins or becoming greenish, surrounding small greenish cream flower heads, all summer and into September. Profusion of red strawberry-like fruits.","image":"","commonName":"kousa 'Eurostar'","nurseriesCount":1,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":366111,"botanicalName":"<em>Cornus</em> <em>kousa</em> 'Galilean'","entityDescription":"A deciduous small tree or large shrub with a spreading habit and pointed, oval-shaped, dark glossy green foliage turning to shades of red and purple in the autumn.  White flowers (bracts) appear in early to mid-summer, followed by strawberry-like pink berries in the autumn","image":"","commonName":"kousa [Galilean]","nurseriesCount":4,"synonymParentPlantId":204398,"synonymParentPlantName":"<em>Cornus</em> <em>kousa</em> <span style=\"font-variant: small-caps;\">Galilean</span> ('Galzam')","isAgm":false,"isSynonym":true,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":278136,"botanicalName":"<em>Cornus</em> <em>kousa</em> 'Galzam'","entityDescription":"A deciduous small tree or large shrub with a spreading habit and pointed, oval-shaped, dark glossy green foliage turning to shades of red and purple in the autumn.  White flowers (bracts) appear in early to mid-summer, followed by strawberry-like pink berries in the autumn","image":"","commonName":"kousa [Galilean]","nurseriesCount":4,"synonymParentPlantId":204398,"synonymParentPlantName":"<em>Cornus</em> <em>kousa</em> <span style=\"font-variant: small-caps;\">Galilean</span> ('Galzam')","isAgm":false,"isSynonym":true,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":150345,"botanicalName":"<em>Cornus</em> <em>kousa</em> 'Gold Cup' (v)","entityDescription":"A deciduous shrub or small tree with oval-shaped dark green foliage, variegated with a bright golden yellow patch in the cen