 to late summer, followed by woody, rounded, olive-green fruit","image":"","commonName":"cider gum [Silverana]","nurseriesCount":14,"synonymParentPlantId":374994,"synonymParentPlantName":"<em>Eucalyptus</em> <em>gunnii</em> <span style=\"font-variant: small-caps;\">Silverana</span> ('Lon40')","isAgm":false,"isSynonym":true,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":121876,"botanicalName":"<em>Eucalyptus</em> <em>gunnii</em> 'Silver Drop'","entityDescription":"A medium sized evergreen tree reaching a height of 25m (83⅓ft) when mature. The smooth bark is grey, with orange and pink hues. It is a useful subject for wetter soils, tolerating it better than most eucalypts.  The round to oval, juvenile leaves are arranged in opposite pairs and are a bright, silvery blue-green. Adult foliage is sickle-shaped and blue green. White flowers are produced in spring. All parts of the plant are aromatic","image":"","commonName":null,"nurseriesCount":2,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":263244,"botanicalName":"<em>Eucalyptus</em> <em>gunnii</em> <span style=\"font-variant: small-caps;\">Azura</span> ('Cagire'<sup>PBR</sup>)","entityDescription":"Hardier and bushier than the species, an aromatic, evergreen shrub or small tree with silvery-grey bark peeling to reveal cream, olive green, or pinkish brown patches. Lance-shaped mature foliage is greyish blue-green; rounded juvenile foliage is silvery. Small, white, fragrant, fluffy flowers appear on mature plants from mid-summer into autumn, followed by woody, rounded, olive-green fruit","image":"_KOS2272(1).jpg","commonName":"cider gum [Azura]","nurseriesCount":18,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":374994,"botanicalName":"<em>Eucalyptus</em> <em>gunnii</em> <span style=\"font-variant: small-caps;\">Silverana</span> ('Lon40')","entityDescription":"An aromatic, evergreen tree with silvery-grey bark peeling to reveal cream or pinkish brown patches. Lance-shaped mature foliage is blue-green; rounded juvenile foliage is silvery-blue. Small, white, fragrant, fluffy flowers appear on mature plants in mid- to late summer, followed by woody, rounded, olive-green fruit","image":"","commonName":"cider gum [Silverana]","nurseriesCount":14,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":6889,"botanicalName":"<em>Eucalyptus</em> <em>gunnii</em> subsp. <em>archeri</em>","entityDescription":"A medium-sized, evergreen tree about 12-15m tall, with smooth grey and white bark, sometimes with patches of pink or pale green. Juvenile foliage is broadly oval and grey-green, on purple-flushed stems; adult leaves are more narrowly oval and greener. Flowers white, fluffy, in small clusters","image":"MAR0021606_8129.jpg","commonName":"alpine cider gum","nurseriesCount":3,"synonymParentPlantId":6878,"synonymParentPlantName":"<em>Eucalyptus</em> <em>archeri</em>","isAgm":false,"isSynonym":true,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":6890,"botanicalName":"<em>Eucalyptus</em> <em>kybeanensis</em>","entityDescription":"An evergreen tree, usually growing to no more than 7m (23ft) in the UK. bark is a rich chocolate brown with white striations, which when shed exposes lighter brown bark beneath. Juvenile foliage is lance-shaped and a bronze purple when young maturing to dark green. Adult foliage is lance-shaped and a glossy dark green. The foliage is lightly aromatic. White flowers are produced from late autumn through winter and are honey-scented.  A high altitude eucalyptus in its native habitat, it can tolerate colder gardens in the UK well once mature, provided the soil is well drained.","image":"","commonName":"Kybean mallee ash","nurseriesCount":1,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":21834,"botanicalName":"<em>Eucalyptus</em> <em>moorei</em>","entityDescription":"A fast-growing evergreen tree reaching a height of 6-7m (20-23ft) in height if allowed to grow naturally. The smooth, highly ornamental bark is silver and cinnamon brown with cream striations and is regularly shed in strips, to reveal white bark beneath. The ovate, juvenile foliage is blue-green aging to a glossy rich green. Adult foliage is sickle shaped and glossy green with bright goleden yellow petioles. The foliage is strongly aromatic. Large groups of golden yellow buds, often up to 15 in a cluster, open to reveal creamy-white flowers in autumn","image":"","commonName":"narrow-leaved Sally","nurseriesCount":1,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":82652,"botanicalName":"<em>Eucalyptus</em> <em>moorei</em> var. <em>nana</em>","entityDescription":"A fast-growing evergreen tree reaching a height of 6-7m (20-23ft) in height if allowed to grow naturally. The smooth, highly ornamental bark is silver and cinnamon brown with cream striations and is regularly shed in strips, to reveal white bark beneath. The ovate, juvenile foliage is blue-green aging to a glossy rich green. Adult foliage is sickle shaped and glossy green with bright goleden yellow petioles. The foliage is strongly aromatic. Large groups of golden yellow buds, often up to 15 in a cluster, open to reveal creamy-white flowers in autumn","image":"","commonName":"narrow-leaved Sally","nurseriesCount":1,"synonymParentPlantId":21834,"synonymParentPlantName":"<em>Eucalyptus</em> <em>moorei</em>","isAgm":false,"isSynonym":true,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":6892,"botanicalName":"<em>Eucalyptus</em> <em>neglecta</em>","entityDescription":"A fast-growing, evergreen tree when young, although growth slows down as the tree ages. It reaches a mature height of around 10m (33ft) The smooth bark can vary in colour from yellow-green to greyish-brown. Juvenile leaves are very large, rounded, and green tinged with purple. The adult leaves are broady lance-shaped and mid green. Foliage and young stems are highly aromatic when crushed. Flowers are white and appear in summer, in large clusters of up to fifteen","image":"JFEucalyptusneglecta1.JPG","commonName":"Omeo gum","nurseriesCount":1,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":521465,"botanicalName":"<em>Eucalyptus</em> <em>neglecta</em> 'Dargo Plains'","entityDescription":"A fast-gowing, very hardy evergreen large shrub to tree, reaching a mature height of around 7m.  The very large, highly aromatic, round, jade-green foliage grows to resemble extra-large bay leaves, sometimes with a purple tinge.  The bark is smooth and greenish-yellow to greyish-brown and masses of small, white flowers appear from July to August.  Tolerates wet soils and shady areas and a good choice for a quick-growing screen.  May also provide a roosting area for small birds such as goldfinches in winter .  Foliage may shred in high winds","image":"EucalyptusneglectaDargoPlains.jpg","commonName":null,"nurseriesCount":1,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":6893,"botanicalName":"<em>Eucalyptus</em> <em>nicholii</em>","entityDescription":"A vigorous tree growing to 18m with an open, rounded crown, weeping branches and brown, fissured bark. Linear, pendent juvenile grey-green leaves to 7cm long and narrow adult leaves to 13cm long, are borne on red stems and release a peppermint scent when crushed. Umbels of, typically seven, white flowers are produced in autumn, followed by rounded to bell shaped woody fruits","image":"EucalyptusnicholiiHydeHallDanielBridge6415.jpg","commonName":"Nichol's willow-leafed peppe